ae3ffefa85.caption:
@ramayanamovie has crossed ₹1,000 Crore worldwide in just eight days, grossing ₹1,033.55 Crore by Thursday, November 12, according to Sacnilk. It becomes only the 11th Indian film in the ₹1,000 Crore club, and the third-fastest to get there after Pushpa 2 and Dhurandhar 2.

The film collected ₹53.50 Crore net in India on Day 8, taking its India net total to ₹564.60 Crore, with overseas collections at ₹358.50 Crore. Starring Ranbir Kapoor as Ram, @thenameisyash as Ravana and @saipallavi.senthamarai as Sita, Ramayana is also Ranbir's first film to cross ₹1,000 Crore, surpassing Animal's lifetime collection.

Tag the friend who predicted Ramayana would hit ₹1,000 Crore.

