d5219caf6b.caption:
@ramayanamovie is reportedly getting more screens in Tamil Nadu and Kerala in its second week, according to TrackTollywood. That's a rare feat for a non-local film, since dubbed releases usually lose screens after the first week.

The film's Malayalam version has been a big hit with family audiences. In Kerala, Ramayana collected about ₹21 Crore in six days and from Monday, November 9, overtook Suriya's Scene in daily collections, earning ₹3.90 Crore that day, according to The Week. The epic has now grossed over ₹1,000 Crore worldwide.

